            <ArticleTitle>&quot;Painful and disabling granuloma annulare&quot;: a case of Munchausen by proxy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>363-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the unusual case of a child who from age 6 received fourteen excisions and four grafting procedures in an attempt to control &quot;painful and disabling granuloma annulare.&quot; Although the lesions were considered disabling by the mother, they were nontender on repeated examinations. A careful investigation revealed that the mother was falsely describing symptoms necessitating surgery so she could receive public housing and other benefits for parents with a disabled child. We believe this case should alert the clinician as to the extreme measures imposed on children in Munchausen syndrome by proxy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
